National Presence Across the United States
Across the United States, Chinese-American communities remain heavily concentrated along the Pacific Coast and in major metro areas. While New York State houses 774,426 Chinese-American residents (14.43% of the national total), California has the largest statewide population, led by the San Francisco Bay Area (where Chinese-Americans make up 12.44% of metro residents) and Greater Los Angeles. Large communities have also developed in Seattle, Boston, Chicago, and Houston as new waves of students, professionals, and families settled in these cities over the past several decades.


